# Concurrent pull requests almost always append to the same CHANGELOG section, which git treats as a
# conflict even though the two edits are independent. The built-in "union" merge driver keeps BOTH sides
# instead of stopping, so rebasing a branch after a sibling PR lands resolves itself and nobody has to
# hand-merge a list of bullets (and risk dropping one).
#
# Two things to know:
#   * Keep the "### Added / ### Changed / ### Fixed / ### Internal" headings permanently present under
#     [Unreleased]. Union merges lines, so if two branches each ADD the same heading you get it twice;
#     if the heading is already there, only the new bullets merge and the result is clean.
#   * GitHub does not apply this driver when it computes a pull request's mergeability, so a PR can still
#     be shown as conflicting. Rebasing locally is what resolves it - this makes that rebase automatic.
#     See https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/9288
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
